message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an “interactive card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** – no JavaScript required.

---

## 1️⃣ Markup (HTML)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>This is the back of the card.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

* `card-wrapper` centers the card on the page.  
* Inside we have two faces (`front` and `back`) that will be swapped during rotation.

---

## 2️⃣ Styling (CSS)

Create a file called `style.css` and paste the following:

```css
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the card on the page */
.card-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;          /* full viewport height */
    background: #f0f0f0;
}

/* Card container */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;     /* gives depth to the 3D transform */
    position: relative;
}

/* Common styles for both faces */
.card-face {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: absolute;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the reverse side while rotating */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: white;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
}

/* Front face styling */
.front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* Back face styling */
.back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* start rotated so it's hidden */
}

/* Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
.card:hover .front {
    transform: rotateY(-180deg);
}

.card:hover .back {
    transform: rotateY(0deg);
}
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | `.card` has `perspective: 800px;` – this creates a 3‑D space. |
| 2 | Both `.front` and `.back` are positioned absolutely on top of each other. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden;` hides the backside of each face during rotation. |
| 4 | On hover, the front face rotates `-180deg` (turns away) and the back face rotates to `0deg` (faces the viewer). |
| 5 | `transition: transform 0.6s ease;` makes the flip smooth. |

---

## 🎨 Customization Ideas

| Property | What to change | Example |
|----------|----------------|---------|
| `width / height` | Size of the card | `400px / 250px` |
| `perspective` | Depth of the 3D effect | `1200px` for a more pronounced flip |
| `background` | Color scheme | Use solid colors or images |
| `border-radius` | Rounded corners | `20px` for a softer look |
| `transition-duration` | Speed of the flip | `0.4s` for faster, `0.8s` for slower |

Feel free to copy the code into your project and tweak it as you like! If you need help adding content or making it responsive, just let me know.
